        "metadata": {
          "category": "stories",
          "minAge": 4,
          "maxAge": 8,
          "media": {
            "duration": 1172,
            "fileSize": 18954991
          },
          "author": "Dashka Slater",
          "description": "Join Escargot, the charming French snail, in two delightful stories filled with humor, warmth, and gentle moments perfect for young listeners. Brought to life with music and sound effects, these audiobooks invite kids to slow down and enjoy adventures that celebrate friendship, curiosity, and everyday joys.  \n\nIn one story, Escargot ventures outside after a long winter to search for the first signs of spring, meeting an unexpected new friend along the way and discovering the fun of changing seasons. In the other, Escargot hosts a pajama party where everyone is determined to stay awake—even as bedtime slowly sneaks in. From star-gazing to blanket forts, Escargot does his best to keep the night going.  \n\nCreated by New York Times–bestselling author Dashka Slater and illustrated by former Pixar animator Sydney Hanson, these stories are sweet, funny, and full of personality—perfect for story time, bedtime, or any cozy moment.  \n\nA Macmillan Audio production from Farrar, Straus and Giroux.  \n\nThis collection includes:\nEscargot and the Search for Spring\nGood Night, Escargot",
          "abridged": false,
          "audioPreviewUrl": "https://audio-previews-media.api.yotoplay.com/audio-previews/1b1131905d998c7e167e6f245e007ecbcfa0a8c88ec30ad8016e4a5962aea9d4/7zK8DqcuYJurBHxpJJF1P4XMlcn-xoqra8jUdMANEFo.mp3",
